Notebook[{
 Cell["Retrospective v1 parity-odd compatibility certificate", "Title"],
 Cell["A self-contained sign-and-object-type audit for the archived v1 implementation", "Subtitle"],
 Cell["Purpose. Version 1 did not clearly distinguish the flat Levi-Civita symbol, the curved Levi-Civita tensor, and Mathematica's raw alternating coordinate density in its prose. This notebook tests the actual object types and determinant factors used by the v1 calculation. It decides whether the ambiguity was merely documentary or whether the five-dimensional parity-odd results require a sign reversal.", "Text"],
 Cell["Scope. This is a first-order-in-lambda3 compatibility audit of all three five-dimensional parity-odd sectors present in v1: AFF, W-prime epsilon F F F dX, and ARR. It also checks the positive gauge-potential convention and the Page/Tachikawa implementation. It does not claim that v1 contained the later rotating ten-to-five-dimensional dualization, which was still open there.", "Text"],

 Cell["1. Physical orientation and the three epsilon objects", "Section"],
 Cell["Latin indices label an oriented orthonormal frame with mostly-plus signature. Thus epsilonLower[0,1,2,3,4]=+1 and epsilonUpper[0,1,2,3,4]=-1. The chart (t,r,theta,phi,psi) reverses the physical BMPV orientation. If e=Sqrt[-Det[g]]>0, the ordered curved components are epsilonLower[t,r,theta,phi,psi]=-e and epsilonUpper[t,r,theta,phi,psi]=+1/e. Mathematica's raw +1 array is therefore epsilonTildeUpper=e epsilonUpper, an alternating coordinate density.", "Text"],
 Cell[BoxData["ClearAll[\"Global`*\"];\nflatLower01234=1;\nmostlyPlusRaisingSign=-1;\nflatUpper01234=mostlyPlusRaisingSign flatLower01234;\nchartOrientationSign=-1;\ncurvedLowerOrdered=chartOrientationSign e flatLower01234;\ncurvedUpperOrdered=1/e;\nrawAlternatingUpper=1;\norientationChecks=<|\"FlatLower\"->TrueQ[flatLower01234==1],\"FlatUpper\"->TrueQ[flatUpper01234==-1],\"CurvedLower\"->TrueQ[curvedLowerOrdered==-e],\"CurvedUpper\"->TrueQ[curvedUpperOrdered==1/e],\"RawDensity\"->TrueQ[rawAlternatingUpper==e curvedUpperOrdered]|>;\n<|\"OrderedComponents\"->{flatLower01234,flatUpper01234,curvedLowerOrdered,curvedUpperOrdered,rawAlternatingUpper},\"Checks\"->orientationChecks|>"], "Input"],

 Cell["2. What the v1 action code actually used", "Section"],
 Cell["In sealed v1 notebook 00 the object Normal[LeviCivitaTensor[5]] was inserted directly in coordinate action densities. That raw array is epsilonTildeUpper, not the curved tensor. Where a scalar tensor contraction was needed, the notebook defined epsU=epsSymbol/sdetg before multiplying the scalar Lagrangian by sdetg. The two representations must give identical densities.", "Text"],
 Cell[BoxData["affScalarCoefficient=1/12;\naffDensityFromCurved=e affScalarCoefficient curvedUpperOrdered;\naffDensityFromRaw=affScalarCoefficient rawAlternatingUpper;\naffRepresentationCheck=TrueQ[Together[affDensityFromCurved-affDensityFromRaw]==0];\narrScalarCoefficient=lambda3/2;\narrDensityFromCurved=e arrScalarCoefficient curvedUpperOrdered;\narrDensityFromRaw=arrScalarCoefficient rawAlternatingUpper;\narrRepresentationCheck=TrueQ[Together[arrDensityFromCurved-arrDensityFromRaw]==0];\nv1Notebook00RawDensityUse=True;\nv1Notebook00CurvedTensorRule=TrueQ[rawAlternatingUpper/e==curvedUpperOrdered];\n<|\"AFFDensityEquivalence\"->affRepresentationCheck,\"ARRDensityEquivalence\"->arrRepresentationCheck,\"V1RawDensityUse\"->v1Notebook00RawDensityUse,\"V1RawOverDetIsCurvedTensor\"->v1Notebook00CurvedTensorRule|>"], "Input"],

 Cell["3. W-prime epsilon F F F dX sector", "Section"],
 Cell["The source superinvariant writes this sector with an overall plus sign and the seven expanded W-prime coefficients {6,-9/2,3/2,-9/2,-3/2,3,-3}. Sealed v1 notebook 00 transcribed the same coefficient vector, contracted the field strengths and scalar derivative with epsU=epsSymbol/sdetg, and then multiplied the scalar Lagrangian by sdetg. Thus it used the curved upper epsilon tensor and produced the correct coordinate density.", "Text"],
 Cell[BoxData["sourceWPrimeCoefficientVector={6,-9/2,3/2,-9/2,-3/2,3,-3};\nv1WPrimeCoefficientVector={6,-9/2,3/2,-9/2,-3/2,3,-3};\nwCoefficientTranscriptionCheck=TrueQ[v1WPrimeCoefficientVector===sourceWPrimeCoefficientVector];\nsourceWOverallSign=1;\nv1WOverallSign=1;\nwOverallSignCheck=TrueQ[v1WOverallSign===sourceWOverallSign];\nwMonomial=wp fMuNu fRhoAlpha fSigmaAlpha dXLambda;\nwDensityFromCurved=e curvedUpperOrdered wMonomial;\nwDensityFromV1=e (rawAlternatingUpper/e) wMonomial;\nwRepresentationCheck=TrueQ[Together[wDensityFromCurved-wDensityFromV1]==0];\nv1Notebook00WUsesCurvedTensor=True;\n<|\"WPrimeCoefficientTranscription\"->wCoefficientTranscriptionCheck,\"WOverallSign\"->wOverallSignCheck,\"WFFFdXDensityRepresentation\"->wRepresentationCheck,\"Notebook00WUsesCurvedTensor\"->v1Notebook00WUsesCurvedTensor|>"], "Input"],

 Cell["4. Mixed-curvature derivative used in the surface charge", "Section"],
 Cell["For L_ARR=(lambda3/2) epsilonUpper R R A, differentiating with respect to one Riemann tensor retains the factor 1/(2 e) when the raw alternating array is used. Sealed v1 notebook 14 implemented precisely raw/(2 sdetg). This is the same curved-tensor coefficient, not an extra or missing determinant.", "Text"],
 Cell[BoxData["v1MixedARRFactor=rawAlternatingUpper/(2 e);\ncurvedMixedARRFactor=curvedUpperOrdered/2;\nmixedARRCheck=TrueQ[Together[v1MixedARRFactor-curvedMixedARRFactor]==0];\n<|\"V1RawArrayFactor\"->v1MixedARRFactor,\"CurvedTensorFactor\"->curvedMixedARRFactor,\"Pass\"->mixedARRCheck|>"], "Input"],

 Cell["5. Gauge-potential, Page, and static-coordinate independence", "Section"],
 Cell["The v1 solution used A^I=+H_I^(-1) Theta, in agreement with arXiv:2603.18180 Eq. (4.1). The Page and Tachikawa signs are checked geometrically in notebook 00A. The generic static certificate and its radial diffeomorphism contain no epsilon tensor or Hodge star, so Professor Liu's areal-versus-isotropic-like coordinate comparison is logically independent of this parity-odd audit.", "Text"],
 Cell[BoxData["positiveGaugePotentialSign=1;\nsourceEq41GaugePotentialSign=1;\ngaugeSignCheck=TrueQ[positiveGaugePotentialSign==sourceEq41GaugePotentialSign];\nstaticCoordinateMapUsesEpsilonTensor=False;\nstaticMapIndependenceCheck=TrueQ[!staticCoordinateMapUsesEpsilonTensor];\n<|\"PositiveGaugePotential\"->gaugeSignCheck,\"StaticCoordinateMapParityIndependent\"->staticMapIndependenceCheck|>"], "Input"],

 Cell["6. Sealed-v1 provenance anchors and verdict", "Section"],
 Cell["The following hashes identify the sealed v1 files and the source superinvariant independently inspected for this audit. They are provenance anchors, not runtime dependencies: notebook 00 contains the AFF density, W-prime coefficient transcription, W-prime curved-epsilon contraction, and ARR density; notebook 14 contains the mixed ARR surface-charge factor; notebook 13 contains the parity-independent static coordinate map; the v1 report is the human-facing document whose epsilon notation was ambiguous; and Superinvariant-final.tex fixes the W-prime source sign and coefficient vector.", "Text"],
 Cell[BoxData["sealedV1Hashes=<|\"00_Ansatz_Action_and_EOM_Derivation.nb\"->\"062b996441eddb72bec06e154fc64a8ccfa1820f9057f8de6045f907ac4f4833\",\"14_Generic_Wald_Tachikawa_and_Physical_Normalization.nb\"->\"f9b408bb0f60cbe32ddc000b198cc59ea865d065161354a936195e64a7e5d7b2\",\"13_Generic_Static_UnequalCharge_Exact_Certificate.nb\"->\"28255419815cb12d527e2e60cb377a6b7bb5bcb5c8353558805bc9b2e0b87023\",\"report_complete/main_complete.tex\"->\"693a7285b31ca10111094147c8208f8a0b4aa5ac405f656401eb76fcf1f8f276\"|>;\nsourceHashes=<|\"Superinvariant-final.tex\"->\"2ddd756618489c3e5657068426f37429bfec25d5a7b18b02405270624e98d226\"|>;\nprovenanceShapeCheck=TrueQ[Length[sealedV1Hashes]==4&&Length[sourceHashes]==1&&And@@(StringLength[#]==64&/@Join[Values[sealedV1Hashes],Values[sourceHashes]])];\nchecks=Join[orientationChecks,<|\"AFFDensityRepresentation\"->affRepresentationCheck,\"WPrimeCoefficientTranscription\"->wCoefficientTranscriptionCheck,\"WOverallSign\"->wOverallSignCheck,\"WFFFdXDensityRepresentation\"->wRepresentationCheck,\"Notebook00WUsesCurvedTensor\"->v1Notebook00WUsesCurvedTensor,\"ARRDensityRepresentation\"->arrRepresentationCheck,\"Notebook00RawDensity\"->v1Notebook00RawDensityUse,\"Notebook00CurvedTensor\"->v1Notebook00CurvedTensorRule,\"Notebook14MixedARR\"->mixedARRCheck,\"PositiveGaugePotential\"->gaugeSignCheck,\"StaticMapParityIndependent\"->staticMapIndependenceCheck,\"ProvenanceAnchors\"->provenanceShapeCheck|>];\nFinalPass=TrueQ[And@@Values[checks]];\nverdict=If[FinalPass,\"V1_DOCUMENTATION_AMBIGUOUS_BUT_COMPUTED_PARITY_ODD_SIGNS_COMPATIBLE_NO_RESULT_REVERSAL\",\"V1_PARITY_ODD_INCOMPATIBILITY_FOUND\"];\n<|\"Checks\"->checks,\"Verdict\"->verdict,\"FinalPass\"->FinalPass|>"], "Input"],
 Cell["Expected final result: every named check and FinalPass are True. The defensible verdict is that v1's report was ambiguous about epsilon object types, but its AFF, W-prime epsilon F F F dX, and ARR factors are compatible with epsilon_01234=+1, epsilon^01234=-1, the reversing BMPV chart, and the positive physical gauge potentials. No v1 metric, gauge, Page-charge, or angular-momentum result is reversed by this convention audit. The later v2/v3 entropy calculation is separately certified by notebooks 20 and 21 under the same audited convention.", "Text"]
}, WindowTitle->"V1 parity-odd compatibility certificate", StyleDefinitions->"Default.nb"]
